1
00:00:10,008 --> 00:00:11,508
Scene 1: Planning a Trip

2
00:00:11,508 --> 00:00:17,459
I'm thinking of going on a trip during my next break.

3
00:00:17,482 --> 00:00:20,115
That sounds great!

4
00:00:20,138 --> 00:00:23,615
Where are you planning to go?

5
00:00:23,638 --> 00:00:27,872
I want to go to Hokkaido.

6
00:00:27,895 --> 00:00:32,995
Hokkaido might be cold, you know.

7
00:00:33,018 --> 00:00:39,359
Yeah, that's why I need to buy a warm coat.

8
00:00:39,382 --> 00:00:43,050
Are you planning to go skiing?

9
00:00:43,073 --> 00:00:49,506
Yes, I’ll go skiing and soak in hot springs.

10
00:00:49,529 --> 00:00:53,362
Hot springs sound amazing.

11
00:00:53,385 --> 00:00:58,519
I haven’t bought my plane tickets yet.

12
00:00:58,542 --> 00:01:02,775
You should buy them soon.

13
00:01:02,798 --> 00:01:05,558
You're right.

14
00:01:05,581 --> 00:01:10,048
Have you booked a hotel?

15
00:01:10,071 --> 00:01:15,771
Yes, I reserved one online.

16
00:01:15,794 --> 00:01:19,060
That’s great!

17
00:01:19,083 --> 00:01:24,717
Do you know any delicious foods in Hokkaido?

18
00:01:24,740 --> 00:01:29,292
Crab and ramen are really tasty there.

19
00:01:29,315 --> 00:01:32,082
I see.

20
00:01:32,106 --> 00:01:36,410
I definitely want to try them.

21
00:01:36,433 --> 00:01:41,151
Shall I look up some famous restaurants for you?

22
00:01:41,174 --> 00:01:44,091
Thank you so much.

23
00:01:44,115 --> 00:01:46,848
Please do.

24
00:01:46,871 --> 00:01:51,371
Don’t forget to take lots of photos!

25
00:01:51,394 --> 00:01:56,327
Yeah, I’ll bring my new camera.

26
00:01:56,350 --> 00:02:00,490
Have a safe trip!

27
00:02:00,514 --> 00:02:03,148
Thank you so much.

28
00:02:03,171 --> 00:02:07,404
I’ll bring back some souvenirs.

29
00:02:07,427 --> 00:02:10,527
I’m looking forward to it!

30
00:02:10,550 --> 00:02:14,696
Is there anything you want me to bring?

31
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:18,687
I’d love some sweet snacks.

32
00:02:18,710 --> 00:02:21,577
Got it.

33
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:24,833
I’ll bring them back for you.

34
00:02:24,856 --> 00:02:28,123
Thank you so much.

35
00:02:28,146 --> 00:02:37,155
The script for today’s video is available for download in the description and top comments. Please leave a comment before downloading!

36
00:02:37,155 --> 00:02:38,655
Scene 2: PC Troubles and an Alternative Solution

37
00:02:38,655 --> 00:02:43,088
My computer broke down.

38
00:02:43,111 --> 00:02:47,450
Really? That’s awful.

39
00:02:47,473 --> 00:02:50,782
What happened?

40
00:02:50,806 --> 00:02:55,440
The screen suddenly went dark.

41
00:02:55,464 --> 00:02:59,297
That’s terrible.

42
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:04,187
I need to write a report.

43
00:03:04,210 --> 00:03:07,989
When’s the deadline?

44
00:03:08,012 --> 00:03:11,996
Tomorrow morning.

45
00:03:12,020 --> 00:03:16,554
You’d better hurry then.

46
00:03:16,577 --> 00:03:21,344
I’ll try getting it repaired.

47
00:03:21,367 --> 00:03:26,918
But I’m not sure if it’ll be fixed today.

48
00:03:26,941 --> 00:03:30,575
What should I do?

49
00:03:30,598 --> 00:03:35,968
You can use my computer if you’d like.

50
00:03:35,991 --> 00:03:38,703
Really? That’d be a huge help.

51
00:03:38,726 --> 00:03:41,400
Thank you so much.

52
00:03:41,423 --> 00:03:45,608
Where will you write the report?

53
00:03:45,632 --> 00:03:49,932
I’m thinking of writing it at the library.

54
00:03:49,955 --> 00:03:55,189
I'll bring my laptop now.

55
00:03:55,212 --> 00:03:58,248
Excuse me.

56
00:03:58,271 --> 00:04:01,571
Please don’t worry about it.

57
00:04:01,594 --> 00:04:05,261
When should I return it?

58
00:04:05,284 --> 00:04:09,596
Tomorrow afternoon would be fine.

59
00:04:09,620 --> 00:04:12,486
That’s a huge help.

60
00:04:12,509 --> 00:04:16,809
Is the data for the report okay?

61
00:04:16,833 --> 00:04:21,866
Yes, I saved it on a USB drive.

62
00:04:21,889 --> 00:04:25,671
Great, that puts my mind at ease.

63
00:04:25,695 --> 00:04:31,270
I’ll take the laptop to the repair shop later.

64
00:04:31,293 --> 00:04:34,427
I hope it gets fixed.

65
00:04:34,450 --> 00:04:38,998
Yeah, I’d be in trouble if it didn’t.

66
00:04:39,021 --> 00:04:43,597
See you later.

67
00:04:43,621 --> 00:04:47,291
Thank you so much!

68
00:04:47,315 --> 00:04:51,948
Good luck with your report!

69
00:04:51,971 --> 00:04:56,071
Yes, I’ll write it in a hurry.

70
00:04:56,094 --> 00:04:59,202
Take care.

71
00:04:59,226 --> 00:05:06,331
You can find a link to the site for reviewing today’s lesson in the description and top comment. *Note: The site may be removed without notice.

72
00:05:06,331 --> 00:05:07,831
Scene 3: Ordering at a Restaurant

73
00:05:07,831 --> 00:05:12,931
This is my first time here.

74
00:05:12,954 --> 00:05:17,187
There’s so much on the menu!

75
00:05:17,210 --> 00:05:21,277
What’s good here?

76
00:05:21,300 --> 00:05:27,000
My friend said the curry is delicious.

77
00:05:27,023 --> 00:05:32,357
I’ll try the curry then.

78
00:05:32,380 --> 00:05:37,379
I think I’ll go for the hamburger.

79
00:05:37,402 --> 00:05:41,269
That looks good too.

80
00:05:41,292 --> 00:05:45,725
Should we order drinks too?

81
00:05:45,748 --> 00:05:49,582
I’d like some coffee.

82
00:05:49,605 --> 00:05:53,556
I’ll have tea.

83
00:05:53,579 --> 00:05:58,552
Excuse me, we’d like to order, please.

84
00:05:58,576 --> 00:06:04,276
One curry and one hamburger, please.

85
00:06:04,299 --> 00:06:10,016
After the meal, we’d like coffee and tea.

86
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:14,106
I’d like dessert too.

87
00:06:14,129 --> 00:06:17,963
There’s cake available.

88
00:06:17,986 --> 00:06:22,052
Chocolate cake sounds perfect.

89
00:06:22,075 --> 00:06:28,309
I might be too full after this.

90
00:06:28,332 --> 00:06:33,510
Should we just get one cake then?

91
00:06:33,533 --> 00:06:37,367
Sure, that works.

92
00:06:37,390 --> 00:06:41,223
Let’s split it in half.

93
00:06:41,246 --> 00:06:43,913
Thank you so much.

94
00:06:43,936 --> 00:06:48,131
Is the curry too spicy?

95
00:06:48,154 --> 00:06:53,054
No, it’s just the right level of spice.

96
00:06:53,077 --> 00:06:57,212
The hamburger is really delicious too.

97
00:06:57,235 --> 00:07:02,594
Next time, I’d like to try the hamburger too.

98
00:07:02,618 --> 00:07:06,763
Yeah, you should definitely try it!

99
00:07:06,787 --> 00:07:11,142
The restaurant is nice and quiet too.

100
00:07:11,166 --> 00:07:14,999
Let’s come here together again.

101
00:07:15,022 --> 00:07:18,934
Yes, let’s make that a promise.

102
00:07:18,958 --> 00:07:22,591
Thank you for the meal!

103
00:07:22,614 --> 00:07:27,173
Next time, let’s invite some other friends too.

104
00:07:27,197 --> 00:07:31,972
Yeah, I’d love for everyone to come!

105
00:07:31,995 --> 00:07:33,495
Scene 4: Cleaning Day / How to Organize and Tidy Up

106
00:07:33,495 --> 00:07:38,446
The room is a mess, isn't it?

107
00:07:38,469 --> 00:07:43,814
I've been too busy this week.

108
00:07:43,838 --> 00:07:48,271
Let's clean up together today.

109
00:07:48,294 --> 00:07:53,594
Sure! What can I do to help?

110
00:07:53,617 --> 00:07:58,584
Could you gather the trash for me?

111
00:07:58,607 --> 00:08:02,240
Got it.

112
00:08:02,263 --> 00:08:07,497
Should we separate burnable and non-burnable waste?

113
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:13,153
Yes, please put them in separate bags.

114
00:08:13,176 --> 00:08:17,409
What about plastic bottles?

115
00:08:17,432 --> 00:08:22,799
Please wash them and put them in that box.

116
00:08:22,823 --> 00:08:27,889
Can I open the window?

117
00:08:27,912 --> 00:08:33,023
Yeah, let's air the room out.

118
00:08:33,047 --> 00:08:37,347
I'll tidy up the table too.

119
00:08:37,370 --> 00:08:42,403
I'll vacuum the floor.

120
00:08:42,426 --> 00:08:46,360
The vacuum looks heavy.

121
00:08:46,383 --> 00:08:52,216
Don't worry—I'll handle it.

122
00:08:52,239 --> 00:08:56,623
When are we supposed to take out the trash?

123
00:08:56,646 --> 00:09:01,984
We have to take it out tomorrow morning.

124
00:09:02,008 --> 00:09:07,043
I'll put it by the door then.

125
00:09:07,066 --> 00:09:09,766
Please do.

126
00:09:09,789 --> 00:09:16,181
Should we clean the fridge too?

127
00:09:16,204 --> 00:09:19,002
You're right.

128
00:09:19,026 --> 00:09:23,859
Please throw away any old food.

129
00:09:23,882 --> 00:09:29,116
The milk is past its expiration date.

130
00:09:29,139 --> 00:09:34,527
Okay, I'll toss that out too.

131
00:09:34,550 --> 00:09:39,069
It's looking much cleaner now!

132
00:09:39,092 --> 00:09:43,926
Yeah, I feel great.

133
00:09:43,949 --> 00:09:49,782
Want to grab some coffee after we finish cleaning?

134
00:09:49,805 --> 00:09:53,351
That sounds great!

135
00:09:53,375 --> 00:09:57,208
I'll make it.

136
00:09:57,231 --> 00:10:02,398
Thanks for the coffee!

137
00:10:02,421 --> 00:10:08,554
Coffee after cleaning is the best.

138
00:10:08,577 --> 00:10:10,077
Scene 5: Preparing for a Birthday Party

139
00:10:10,077 --> 00:10:15,848
Tomorrow’s my friend’s birthday party.

140
00:10:15,872 --> 00:10:20,805
Yeah! Are you all set with the preparations?

141
00:10:20,829 --> 00:10:25,019
I’ve already bought the drinks.

142
00:10:25,043 --> 00:10:28,910
What about the food?

143
00:10:28,934 --> 00:10:33,703
I’m planning to cook it now.

144
00:10:33,726 --> 00:10:37,993
Need any help?

145
00:10:38,016 --> 00:10:43,053
Could you chop the vegetables for me?

146
00:10:43,076 --> 00:10:48,015
Should I cut them small?

147
00:10:48,039 --> 00:10:53,150
Yes, please cut them so they’re easy to eat.

148
00:10:53,174 --> 00:10:57,640
Did you reserve the cake?

149
00:10:57,663 --> 00:11:03,497
Yep, I reserved it at the bakery near the station.

150
00:11:03,520 --> 00:11:08,091
What time are we picking it up tomorrow?

151
00:11:08,114 --> 00:11:12,218
I’m planning to go at 3 PM.

152
00:11:12,242 --> 00:11:16,708
Want me to pick it up for you?

153
00:11:16,731 --> 00:11:19,698
Really? That’d be great!

154
00:11:19,721 --> 00:11:23,692
Is it okay if I ask you to do that?

155
00:11:23,716 --> 00:11:28,149
Of course, no problem!

156
00:11:28,172 --> 00:11:33,925
I’ll hand you the reservation slip then.

157
00:11:33,949 --> 00:11:36,815
Got it.

158
00:11:36,838 --> 00:11:40,828
What about decorations for the room?

159
00:11:40,852 --> 00:11:44,960
I’d love to decorate with some flowers.

160
00:11:44,984 --> 00:11:49,763
Let’s buy some cute flowers at the florist!

161
00:11:49,786 --> 00:11:54,620
I’m sure they’ll love it!

162
00:11:54,643 --> 00:11:58,509
Have you bought the gift yet?

163
00:11:58,532 --> 00:12:03,799
Yes, I’m thinking of giving them a book.

164
00:12:03,822 --> 00:12:06,937
What kind of book?

165
00:12:06,960 --> 00:12:11,549
A cookbook for making sweets.

166
00:12:11,573 --> 00:12:14,921
That sounds great!

167
00:12:14,944 --> 00:12:19,463
I can’t wait for tomorrow!

168
00:12:19,486 --> 00:12:23,753
I wish tomorrow would come sooner.

169
00:12:23,776 --> 00:12:28,162
I can’t wait to see my friends!

170
00:12:28,186 --> 00:12:33,579
Yes! Let’s make it an amazing party!

171
00:12:33,602 --> 00:12:35,102
Scene 6: Job Interview Conversation

172
00:12:35,102 --> 00:12:38,135
Excuse me.

173
00:12:38,158 --> 00:12:41,592
Please, have a seat.

174
00:12:41,615 --> 00:12:44,768
Thank you so much.

175
00:12:44,791 --> 00:12:49,424
First, could you tell me your name?

176
00:12:49,447 --> 00:12:54,381
I’m Rin.

177
00:12:54,404 --> 00:12:58,583
When did you come to Japan?

178
00:12:58,606 --> 00:13:03,003
I arrived in April of last year.

179
00:13:03,027 --> 00:13:07,927
How well do you speak Japanese?

180
00:13:07,950 --> 00:13:13,983
I think I can handle everyday conversations.

181
00:13:14,006 --> 00:13:18,539
Do you have any part-time work experience?

182
00:13:18,562 --> 00:13:23,429
I’ve worked at a restaurant before.

183
00:13:23,452 --> 00:13:30,202
This shop gets busy, but are you okay with that?

184
00:13:30,226 --> 00:13:35,941
Yes, I actually prefer busy environments.

185
00:13:35,965 --> 00:13:41,098
How many days a week can you work?

186
00:13:41,121 --> 00:13:46,875
I think I can work three or four days.

187
00:13:46,898 --> 00:13:51,731
Are weekends (Saturday and Sunday) okay?

188
00:13:51,754 --> 00:13:56,265
Yes, no problem at all.

189
00:13:56,289 --> 00:14:01,445
How late can you work in the evening?

190
00:14:01,469 --> 00:14:06,102
I can work until 10 PM.

191
00:14:06,125 --> 00:14:11,158
How will you get to the shop?

192
00:14:11,181 --> 00:14:16,848
I plan to come by bicycle.

193
00:14:16,871 --> 00:14:21,645
How long does it take by bike?

194
00:14:21,668 --> 00:14:26,225
About 15 minutes.

195
00:14:26,248 --> 00:14:29,429
Got it.

196
00:14:29,453 --> 00:14:33,843
Do you have any questions?

197
00:14:33,867 --> 00:14:39,300
Will you provide a uniform?

198
00:14:39,323 --> 00:14:44,590
Yes, we’ll lend you the shop uniform.

199
00:14:44,613 --> 00:14:48,246
Got it.

200
00:14:48,269 --> 00:14:53,989
We’ll let you know the result by phone next week.

201
00:14:54,012 --> 00:14:57,284
Thank you very much.

202
00:14:57,308 --> 00:15:01,008
Please be careful on your way back.

203
00:15:01,031 --> 00:15:04,064
Thank you very much.

204
00:15:04,087 --> 00:15:07,321
Excuse me.

205
00:15:07,344 --> 00:15:08,844
Scene 7: Train Delays and How to Respond

206
00:15:08,844 --> 00:15:13,810
The train isn’t coming anytime soon, huh?

207
00:15:13,833 --> 00:15:17,270
You're right.

208
00:15:17,294 --> 00:15:21,261
What’s going on?

209
00:15:21,284 --> 00:15:25,624
Apparently, it’s delayed due to an accident.

210
00:15:25,648 --> 00:15:30,645
Oh no, that’s a problem.

211
00:15:30,668 --> 00:15:36,368
I might be late for my next class.

212
00:15:36,391 --> 00:15:40,901
You should contact your teacher.

213
00:15:40,925 --> 00:15:43,758
You're right.

214
00:15:43,781 --> 00:15:48,380
I’ll send them an email right now.

215
00:15:48,403 --> 00:15:53,719
I might be late for my part-time job.

216
00:15:53,743 --> 00:15:58,110
Can we take the bus?

217
00:15:58,133 --> 00:16:02,666
Should we head to the bus stop?

218
00:16:02,689 --> 00:16:08,589
But the bus might be crowded too.

219
00:16:08,612 --> 00:16:11,604
You're right.

220
00:16:11,628 --> 00:16:15,895
Should we wait a little longer?

221
00:16:15,918 --> 00:16:20,875
Oh, I can hear an announcement.

222
00:16:20,898 --> 00:16:24,968
Will they resume driving?

223
00:16:24,992 --> 00:16:30,061
They say it’ll start moving again in about ten minutes.

224
00:16:30,085 --> 00:16:35,194
In that case, we’d better wait.

225
00:16:35,218 --> 00:16:39,205
Yeah, let’s do that.

226
00:16:39,228 --> 00:16:44,173
I have an important test today.

227
00:16:44,196 --> 00:16:48,463
That’s worrying.

228
00:16:48,486 --> 00:16:56,953
What if I’m late? I think it’ll be okay if I explain the situation.

229
00:16:56,976 --> 00:17:00,759
I hope so.

230
00:17:00,782 --> 00:17:05,172
Oh, the train’s here!

231
00:17:05,195 --> 00:17:08,262
You’re right.

232
00:17:08,285 --> 00:17:11,791
Let’s hurry and get on!

233
00:17:11,814 --> 00:17:16,157
Let’s get on carefully without pushing.

234
00:17:16,181 --> 00:17:18,547
Okay.

235
00:17:18,570 --> 00:17:22,904
I’m glad we made it in time.

236
00:17:22,927 --> 00:17:26,593
Good luck on your test!

237
00:17:26,616 --> 00:17:30,407
Thank you so much.

238
00:17:30,431 --> 00:17:31,931
Methods to Improve Sleep

239
00:17:31,931 --> 00:17:37,864
I haven’t been sleeping well lately.

240
00:17:37,887 --> 00:17:41,423
What happened?

241
00:17:41,446 --> 00:17:47,146
I’m tired, but I just can’t fall asleep.

242
00:17:47,169 --> 00:17:52,503
Maybe it’s because you’re stressed.

243
00:17:52,526 --> 00:17:56,559
That might be it.

244
00:17:56,582 --> 00:18:03,015
How about drinking warm milk before bed?

245
00:18:03,038 --> 00:18:07,626
That sounds good for the body.

246
00:18:07,650 --> 00:18:12,151
I always do that myself.

247
00:18:12,174 --> 00:18:18,741
Are there any other good methods?

248
00:18:18,764 --> 00:18:24,230
Light exercise might help.

249
00:18:24,253 --> 00:18:27,286
Exercise?

250
00:18:27,309 --> 00:18:32,176
What kind of exercise would be good?

251
00:18:32,199 --> 00:18:38,976
Stretching a little before bed is recommended.

252
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:44,712
Stretching seems doable for me.

253
00:18:44,735 --> 00:18:50,078
Taking a relaxing bath is also good.

254
00:18:50,102 --> 00:18:54,969
I’ve just been taking showers lately.

255
00:18:54,992 --> 00:19:02,307
Soaking in hot water warms up your body.

256
00:19:02,330 --> 00:19:07,430
I’ll try taking a bath tonight.

257
00:19:07,453 --> 00:19:13,891
It’s best not to look at your phone before bed.

258
00:19:13,914 --> 00:19:18,691
I always used to do that in bed.

259
00:19:18,715 --> 00:19:24,303
Eye strain can make it hard to sleep.

260
00:19:24,327 --> 00:19:29,232
I’ll have to be careful about that.

261
00:19:29,255 --> 00:19:33,804
Don’t push yourself too hard.

262
00:19:33,828 --> 00:19:36,542
Thank you so much.

263
00:19:36,566 --> 00:19:43,499
You should take it easy on the weekend.

264
00:19:43,522 --> 00:19:50,000
Yeah, I’m not planning to go anywhere this week.

265
00:19:50,024 --> 00:19:53,290
That sounds like a good idea.

266
00:19:53,313 --> 00:19:57,780
I’ll try going to bed early tonight.

267
00:19:57,803 --> 00:20:02,171
Take care of yourself.

268
00:20:02,195 --> 00:20:04,935
Thank you so much.

269
00:20:04,958 --> 00:20:10,091
Hope you feel better next week!

270
00:20:10,114 --> 00:20:15,381
Yeah, I’ll be careful.

271
00:20:15,405 --> 00:20:16,905
Scene 9: How to Improve Kanji and Conversation Skills

272
00:20:16,905 --> 00:20:22,224
How’s your Japanese learning going?

273
00:20:22,248 --> 00:20:28,681
Kanji is so hard—I just can’t memorize them.

274
00:20:28,704 --> 00:20:33,840
There are so many kanji to learn, after all.

275
00:20:33,864 --> 00:20:39,134
Do you know any good study methods?

276
00:20:39,157 --> 00:20:44,224
Reading books might help.

277
00:20:44,247 --> 00:20:49,913
But I can’t read difficult books.

278
00:20:49,936 --> 00:20:55,803
Comics or children’s books are easier to read.

279
00:20:55,826 --> 00:21:00,746
Ah, that’s a great idea!

280
00:21:00,769 --> 00:21:07,110
Try looking up unknown kanji in a dictionary.

281
00:21:07,134 --> 00:21:12,201
It’s better to read a little every day.

282
00:21:12,223 --> 00:21:17,990
Yeah, consistency is key.

283
00:21:18,013 --> 00:21:22,716
I want to get better at speaking too.

284
00:21:22,740 --> 00:21:28,873
Talking with Japanese friends is the best way.

285
00:21:28,896 --> 00:21:34,165
But I’m embarrassed about making mistakes.

286
00:21:34,189 --> 00:21:38,758
It’s okay to make mistakes.

287
00:21:38,781 --> 00:21:43,414
Hearing that makes me feel better.

288
00:21:43,437 --> 00:21:48,157
Everyone makes mistakes at first.

289
00:21:48,180 --> 00:21:53,514
I really need to build more confidence.

290
00:21:53,537 --> 00:22:00,245
If you’d like, I can help you practice anytime.

291
00:22:00,268 --> 00:22:03,135
Really? That’d be a huge help.

292
00:22:03,158 --> 00:22:06,791
I’d really appreciate that.

293
00:22:06,814 --> 00:22:12,718
Would you like to practice speaking Japanese at a café this weekend?

294
00:22:12,741 --> 00:22:16,713
I’d love to!

295
00:22:16,737 --> 00:22:21,889
Watching the news is also good practice.

296
00:22:21,913 --> 00:22:27,179
The newscasters speak too fast, though.

297
00:22:27,202 --> 00:22:32,751
Try starting with weather forecasts.

298
00:22:32,775 --> 00:22:37,142
Weather forecasts seem doable.

299
00:22:37,165 --> 00:22:42,140
Keep up the hard work!

300
00:22:42,163 --> 00:22:46,714
Yes, I’ll do my best.

301
00:22:46,738 --> 00:22:50,575
I’ll be cheering you on!

302
00:22:50,598 --> 00:22:55,585
I’m looking forward to the café meetup this weekend.

303
00:22:55,609 --> 00:23:00,527
Me too—I can’t wait!

304
00:23:10,558 --> 00:23:12,058
Scene 10: How to Search for Lost Items

305
00:23:12,058 --> 00:23:15,335
Excuse me.

306
00:23:15,359 --> 00:23:19,792
I think I lost my wallet.

307
00:23:19,815 --> 00:23:24,082
Do you know where you might have lost it?

308
00:23:24,105 --> 00:23:29,371
I think it was somewhere in this store.

309
00:23:29,394 --> 00:23:32,828
What does it look like?

310
00:23:32,851 --> 00:23:37,684
It’s black and made of leather.

311
00:23:37,707 --> 00:23:41,807
What was inside it?

312
00:23:41,830 --> 00:23:47,572
It had my credit card and about 10,000 yen.

313
00:23:47,595 --> 00:23:51,267
When do you think you lost it?

314
00:23:51,291 --> 00:23:55,757
I think it was about 30 minutes ago.

315
00:23:55,780 --> 00:23:59,499
Let’s look around for it.

316
00:23:59,522 --> 00:24:02,456
Thank you so much.

317
00:24:02,479 --> 00:24:06,579
I’m really in a tough spot here.

318
00:24:06,602 --> 00:24:11,135
Which seat were you sitting at?

319
00:24:11,158 --> 00:24:14,948
The one near the window.

320
00:24:14,971 --> 00:24:19,438
It wasn’t near your seat.

321
00:24:19,461 --> 00:24:23,455
Maybe you dropped it in the restroom?

322
00:24:23,479 --> 00:24:27,145
Let’s check the restroom too.

323
00:24:27,168 --> 00:24:29,802
Please do.

324
00:24:29,825 --> 00:24:33,162
Oh, this one?

325
00:24:33,185 --> 00:24:36,760
Yes, that one.

326
00:24:36,783 --> 00:24:39,883
This is my wallet.

327
00:24:39,906 --> 00:24:44,273
I found it on the bathroom sink.

328
00:24:44,296 --> 00:24:48,368
Thanks so much for finding it!

329
00:24:48,392 --> 00:24:52,334
Please check the contents.

330
00:24:52,357 --> 00:24:56,902
Yes, everything’s here.

331
00:24:56,926 --> 00:25:00,438
That’s great to hear!

332
00:25:00,462 --> 00:25:04,528
I’ll have to be careful about that.

333
00:25:04,551 --> 00:25:09,710
Yeah, be careful with your belongings.

334
00:25:09,734 --> 00:25:13,478
I really appreciate your help.

335
00:25:13,501 --> 00:25:18,201
From now on, keep it in your bag, okay?

336
00:25:18,224 --> 00:25:22,794
Yes, I absolutely will.